      {
        "finding": "The VO-Rotation training loss sits on a plateau for about 40k updates, then drops sharply (Figure 4, seed 42). No mechanism or head analysis is tied to the drop.",
        "proposed_claim": "Shallow transformers learning a positional copying algorithm show plateau-then-drop loss dynamics; this is not linked to induction heads.",
        "row_ids": []
      },
      {
        "finding": "VO-Rotation accuracy collapses just beyond the period product 5005 (0.0035 and 0.25 at 5008), consistent with residue-based retrieval.",
        "proposed_claim": "Trained VO models use periodic value-side positions for copying.",
